Under Alabama Medicaid Rule No. 560-X-1-.22, when the Agency supersedes a promulgated rule during a state of emergency proclamation, a Provider ALERT must include:

* the effective date of the superseded rule;
* the effective date of the superseding rule;
* the date the superseding rule is to be rescinded;
* the date the superseded rule is to be reinstated;
* the reason for the superseding rule;
* the citation of the superseded rule;
* the citation of the superseding rule;
* the citation of the state of emergency proclamation;
* the citation of the authority to supersede the rule;
* the citation of the authority to issue the Provider ALERT.

